Protein name: Calcium-free alpha-amylase
Organism: Bacillus sp. KSM-K38
PDB ID: 1UD2
Experimental method (X-ray, Cryo-EM, NMR, etc.): X-ray diffraction
Resolution (if available): 2.13 Å
Biological significance: Calcium-free alpha-amylase functions by hydrolyzing alpha-1,4-glucosidic bonds in starch and glycogen to produce sugars like maltose and glucose
